Found while doing karr #73's mutation check, and left alone there because it
is karr #64's, not #73's.

'chunk-header' is one phase covering two distinct ways of running out: the
stream ended where a chunk header belongs with no terminating zero chunk
(_read_line returned undef), and the stream ended inside a chunk header line
(the line came back unterminated). t/read_timeout.t's site pins the phase and
nothing else, so removing either half leaves the other one raising the same
phase and the site still passes.

Measured: commenting out the 'unless defined $line' half of
_assert_chunk_header leaves 'prove -l t/read_timeout.t' PASS (24 tests) while
t/truncated_response.t FAILs. So the defect is covered by the suite as a
whole, and not by the file whose declared job is pairing each read site's two
outcomes.

karr #73 hit exactly this for the new 'header-block' phase, which has the same
two halves, and fixed it there by giving t/read_timeout.t's truncated_ok an
optional 'message => qr/.../' key and passing it at the three head sites. The
same key is already available to the chunk sites; nothing new is needed but
the assertions.

Not urgent -- nothing is unprotected, one file is just weaker than it reads.

Fixed. Both chunk-header sites (buffered _read_chunked and streaming) only ever scripted the 'unterminated line' half; added the 'no terminating zero chunk' half as a new site per pair, plus message => on all four, mirroring k73's header-block fix. Went through the whole file for other two-halved phases with one assertion: only header-block (already fixed) and chunk-header (now fixed, at both its sites) have two croak paths in lib/API/Docker/Role/HTTP.pm -- status-line, chunk-data, chunk-terminator and content-length are single-half phases needing no message. Verified by removing each half of _assert_chunk_header in turn: removing 'unless defined $line' failed only the two new 'never arrives' sites (2/26); removing the unterminated-line half failed only the two 'stops halfway' sites (2/26); restored, prove -lr t/ and dzil test both green. Commit 8ca66aa.
